{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וידבר ה' אל משה", :translit "va-yedabber hashem el mosheh", :gloss "And YHWH spoke to Moses"} {:he "סמך פ' פסח לטהרת לוים", :translit "samakh parashat pesach le-taharat leviyim", :gloss "the section of Pesach is juxtaposed to the purification of Levites"} {:he "רמז שהלוים מפשיטים", :translit "remez she-haleviyim mafshitim", :gloss "a hint that the Levites flay"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut parashiyot) of the Pesach section to the Levite-purification section serves as a textual hint"}], :frame {:text "The Levites' consecration involved shaving all their flesh with a razor and washing their clothes to become ritually pure (Numbers 8:7). Ezekiel 44:11 assigns Levites the responsibility to slaughter burnt offerings and other sacrifices for the house of Israel. Since the Pesach offering requires slaughter and flaying of the animal, the juxtaposition of Numbers 9 (Pesach) immediately after Numbers 8 (Levite purification) hints that the Levites handle the flaying of the Pesach sacrifice.", :sources ["Numbers 8:7" "Ezekiel 44:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut parashiyot) of the Pesach section to the Levite-purification section serves as a textual hint", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:48.624964732Z", :model "glm-5.2"}